    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d105-a2">

                <pb facs="0216" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg136"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Swenson to Mr.
                            Sörensen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Before giving any definite reply to your
                    communication of the 24th instant to Mr. Jules Blom, I beg that you will be good
                    enough to inform me if at the time of your emigration to the United States you
                    had completed your military service, if you secured a permit to emigrate, and if
                    you intend to return to the United States for the purpose of residing and
                    performing the duties of citizenship there.</p>
                <p>Kindly send me your certificate of naturalization, which will be returned to you
                    after examination.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurits S.
                    Swenson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
